-- title:
--   Covariance of Klein's degree-30 form under the half-turn
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $\alpha,\beta,s,n,d\in K$ satisfy the four relations $\alpha\beta=-s$, $2\alpha^{2}=-5-s$, $2\beta^{2}=s-5$ and $s^{2}=5$. Write $T$ for the binary form of degree $30$ defined by $$T(n,d)=n^{30}+522\,n^{25}d^{5}-10005\,n^{20}d^{10}-10005\,n^{10}d^{20}-522\,n^{5}d^{25}+d^{30}.$$ The assertion is the polynomial identity $$T(-\alpha n+\beta d,\ \beta n+\alpha d)=s^{30}\,T(n,d)$$ in $K$. Thus substituting into $T$ the linear forms with matrix $\begin{pmatrix}-\alpha&\beta\\ \beta&\alpha\end{pmatrix}$ reproduces $T$ up to the factor $s^{30}$; equivalently, after dividing the substitution by $s$ (which is nonzero since $s^{2}=5$ and $K$ has characteristic zero), $T$ is strictly invariant. No hypotheses beyond the four relations on $\alpha,\beta,s$ are imposed; $n$ and $d$ are arbitrary, so the conclusion is an identity of polynomials in $n,d$ over the ring generated by $\alpha,\beta,s$ modulo those relations.
--
--   The form $T$ is Klein's icosahedral edge form of degree $30$, and the substitution is the half-turn generator $U=\tfrac1s\begin{pmatrix}-\alpha&\beta\\ \beta&\alpha\end{pmatrix}$ of the binary icosahedral group, realised here over an arbitrary field of characteristic zero by abstract elements satisfying the relations of $\zeta-\zeta^{4}$, $\zeta^{2}-\zeta^{3}$ and $\sqrt5$ for $\zeta$ a primitive fifth root of unity. It is one of the inputs to [`RubinSilverberg.isIcoSymmetry_icoU`](thm.html#RubinSilverberg.isIcoSymmetry_icoU), which records that $U$ is a symmetry of the Rubin–Silverberg datum used for the family of elliptic curves with constant mod-$5$ Galois representation.
